From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: harden ethtool stat strings

Zero each fixed-width ethtool statistic name slot before copying the
name.  This prevents uninitialized bytes in the slot from being exposed
to userspace when the name is shorter than ETH_GSTRING_LEN.

This follows the nss-dp R42 fix for qcom_get_strings().

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_ethtool.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_ethtool.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_ethtool.c
@@ -186,8 +186,9 @@ static void edma_get_strings(struct net_
 		return;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < EDMA_STATS_LEN; i++) {
-		memcpy(data, edma_gstrings_stats[i].stat_string,
-		       strlen(edma_gstrings_stats[i].stat_string));
+		memset(data, 0, ETH_GSTRING_LEN);
+		strscpy(data, edma_gstrings_stats[i].stat_string,
+			ETH_GSTRING_LEN);
 		data += ETH_GSTRING_LEN;
 	}
 
